[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2463079189","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98862#issuecomment-2463079189","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98862","id":2463079189,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Sz5sV","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-07T19:46:45Z","updated_at":"2024-11-07T19:46:45Z","body":"Thanks!\r\n\r\nI'm all for this change at a high-level: it would solve a number of long-running issues that many folks have had with GDExtension. I linked to some of the old issues where this was discussion [in a comment on the proposal](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/9134#issuecomment-1954668943).\r\n\r\nIt's unfortunate that this requires so many little changes throughout `main.cpp` and the non-obvious one to `os_windows.cpp`. That makes me think there's probably going to a bunch of other little regressions that will come out of merging this, that it doesn't catch. So, if we decide to go for this in Godot 4.4, we should probably do it soon: we're still early enough in 4.4's cycle that we could cause and fix a few regressions (but not before 4.4-dev4 since there's already so much merged for that one).\r\n\r\nSkimming through the changes, they _seem_ fine to me.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2463079189/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2463172613","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98862#issuecomment-2463172613","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98862","id":2463172613,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6S0QgF","user":{"login":"HuntJSparra","id":19802403,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODAyNDAz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19802403?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HuntJSparra","html_url":"https://github.com/HuntJSparra","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HuntJSparra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HuntJSparra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HuntJSparra/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HuntJSparra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HuntJSparra/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HuntJSparra/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HuntJSparra/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HuntJSparra/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HuntJSparra/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-07T20:41:41Z","updated_at":"2024-11-07T20:41:41Z","body":"> It's unfortunate that this requires so many little changes throughout `main.cpp` and the non-obvious one to `os_windows.cpp`. That makes me think there's probably going to a bunch of other little regressions that will come out of merging this, that it doesn't catch.\r\n\r\nThat is probably my biggest concern with this. I traced all the affected code-paths I could find and I have a GDExtension+project that tests the loading, but I only have a PC and an older Mac to test on. I can clean up my test project and share it here if that would help people with their review, but, even if those tests pass on all devices, I'd still be worried about edge-cases.\r\n\r\nAll that is to say: I am fine waiting until the next version in order to ensure 4.4's stability.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2463172613/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2463305263","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98862#issuecomment-2463305263","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98862","id":2463305263,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6S0w4v","user":{"login":"HuntJSparra","id":19802403,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODAyNDAz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19802403?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HuntJSparra","html_url":"https://github.com/HuntJSparra","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HuntJSparra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HuntJSparra/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HuntJSparra/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HuntJSparra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HuntJSparra/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HuntJSparra/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HuntJSparra/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HuntJSparra/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HuntJSparra/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-07T21:54:22Z","updated_at":"2024-11-07T21:54:22Z","body":"> I tested this with some GDExtensions on both Linux and Android, including actually using the `ProjectSettings` singleton in `INITIALIZATION_LEVEL_CORE` in the 'godot_openxr_vendors' extension (the use-case there is to not request OpenXR extensions at all if certain project settings aren't enabled -- currently, we have to always request them, but then just avoid using them).\r\n\r\nThe default for the XR project settings are not set until shortly before `INITIALIZATION_LEVEL_SERVERS`, so I suspect this would fail if the extension was somehow added before the project settings were saved for the first time. That is the case for a few hundred project settings (particularly the rendering settings) since I only moved up the settings needed for initialization and the 4 singletons.\r\n\r\nMost of those look safe to move earlier, but I have avoided touching them because it would affect many more parts of the Engine (e.g., many `rendering/` project settings defaults are set by the `RenderingServer`). Still, if people prefer, I can move some or as many as possible earlier.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2463305263/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2463331396","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98862#issuecomment-2463331396","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98862","id":2463331396,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6S03RE","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-07T22:11:14Z","updated_at":"2024-11-07T22:11:14Z","body":"> The default for the XR project settings are not set until shortly before `INITIALIZATION_LEVEL_SERVERS`, so I suspect this would fail if the extension was somehow added before the project settings were saved for the first time. That is the case for a few hundred project settings (particularly the rendering settings) since I only moved up the settings needed for initialization and the 4 singletons.\r\n\r\nThese are project settings coming from the GDExtension, not from Godot. So, it worked fine in my testing :-)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2463331396/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2471287082","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98862#issuecomment-2471287082","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98862","id":2471287082,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TTNkq","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T18:36:02Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T18:36:02Z","body":"Discussed at GDExtension meeting: we think this one will improve this long-standing issue with GDExtension. It could cause subtle bugs that we won't notice until later, so it probably makes sense to merge early in the 4.4 cycle, and we can partially revert or fix issues as the come up before release. `ProjectSettings` is a little tricky because not all settings are available right away, but there is no caching, so they can be requested later; this isn't any worse than `ProjectSettings` not being available at all.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2471287082/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2488994511","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98862#issuecomment-2488994511","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98862","id":2488994511,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UWwrP","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-20T16:08:48Z","updated_at":"2024-11-20T16:08:48Z","body":"> * `OS::has_feature` will still return false for any server feature until `RenderingServer` has been created.\r\n\r\nNot sure if this would be a big deal in practice. However, we may still want to have an early `has_server_feature_callback()` that in debug builds, if verbose enabled, with a `WARN_PRINT_ONCE` or something similar stating that the query can't fall back to the servers at that point. That may help debugging some issues where a maintainer doesn't understand why they are getting `false`. Not sure. Just an idea.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2488994511/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2488995753","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98862#issuecomment-2488995753","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98862","id":2488995753,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UWw-p","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-20T16:09:18Z","updated_at":"2024-11-20T16:09:18Z","body":"Besides my little two comments, overall this looks good and indeed a good tradeoff between benefit and risk of regressions.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2488995753/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2492549964","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98862#issuecomment-2492549964","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98862","id":2492549964,"node_id":"IC_k